{
  "_comment": [
    "Conformance cases for degree-audit requirement evaluation.",
    "Loaded by BOTH mern/client/src/utils/auditRequirements.test.mjs (node --test)",
    "and app/tests/test_audit_requirements.py (pytest). The JS and Python",
    "evaluators are separate implementations of one spec; these cases are what",
    "keeps them honest. If you change semantics on one side, the other side's",
    "suite goes red.",
    "",
    "Shapes are taken from a real UC San Diego audit (Data Science BS, Eighth",
    "College), so the tricky ones are not hypothetical.",
    "",
    "matches() in both runtimes is plain normalized equality for these cases;",
    "cross-listing aliases are the caller's job and are tested separately."
  ],
